# PDFs are binary. Without this, core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) expands
# every LF in the PDF byte stream to CRLF on checkout, so a clean clone produces
# files that differ from what was committed - the 20260519-001 release notes
# checked out 143 bytes larger than their blob. The stored blobs were correct;
# only the working-tree copies were being rewritten.
*.pdf binary
